      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Mimbus.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → a level 3 Barbarian player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Hand Beside the Usurper</strong> — Fawthful's Forces</p><p>Status: Historical actor — present in the 1035 BF false-heir scheme and castle assault; current whereabouts not established</p><p>Mimbus is the operative the historical record places beside Fawthful when the false Bowser Jr. performance gave way to an open assault. The record places Mimbus at the junction between deception, internal betrayal, and the claim that the castle could be turned into a throne for somebody else.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Slam</strong> — “The Hand Beside the Usurper”</li><li><strong>Extra Attack</strong> — “Unknown — hostile operative”</li><li><strong>Crossed the Seam</strong> — “The same figure crossed the seam between the deception and the battle, which makes Mimbus one of the few people who can connect the castle's theatrical lie to its physical breach.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/mimbus</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/mimbus</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
